<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Swedish Guadeloupe</h1><p class="st-meta">1813 CE – 1814 CE · capital Basse-Terre</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Caribbean island promised to Sweden for joining the coalition against Napoleon, nominally Swedish for about a year before returning to France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>British forces captured <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-guadeloupe">French Guadeloupe</a> in 1810. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stockholm-1813">Treaty of Stockholm</a> of 1813, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> ceded the island to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> as a reward for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xiv-john">Crown Prince Charles John</a>, the former French marshal Bernadotte, bringing Sweden into the coalition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Swedish rule was brief and largely nominal. The British garrison remained, and the colonial administration, laws and plantation society based on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> continued with little change.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1814">Treaty of Paris</a> of 1814 restored <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-guadeloupe">Guadeloupe</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In compensation <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> paid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> 24 million francs, money that went into the so-called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadeloupe-fund">Guadeloupe Fund</a>, which paid an annual sum to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xiv-john">Bernadotte</a> family until 1983. The island remains part of France.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1813 CE – 1814 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.78%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1813 CE – 1814 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Basse-Terre</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles XIII</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, Antillean Creole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Guadeloupe (Swedish)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=swedish-guadeloupe" aria-label="Swedish Guadeloupe on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2997 1583 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Swedish Guadeloupe lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3317 1839L3317 1839M3317 1839L5381 440"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3317 1839h0M5381 440h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3317 1839h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3317 1839h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Basse-Terre. <a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=swedish-guadeloupe">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
